<h1>SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT REPORT</h1>
<p style="text-align:center"><b>Student Performance Prediction System (SPPS)</b></p>
<p style="text-align:center">Project Name: EduPredict AI - Student Performance Prediction System<br>Developer: Mansi<br>Date: April 2026<br>Version: 1.0.0</p>

<hr>

<h2>1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY</h2>
<p>The Student Performance Prediction System (SPPS) is a full-stack web application that predicts student academic performance based on various academic indicators. The system uses machine learning algorithms (Linear Regression and Decision Tree logic) to analyze student data including attendance, midterm scores, and previous grades to predict final exam outcomes and identify at-risk students.</p>
<p><b>Key Features:</b></p>
<ul>
<li>Add, edit, and delete student records</li>
<li>Bulk CSV import/export functionality</li>
<li>AI-powered performance prediction</li>
<li>Real-time analytics dashboard</li>
<li>SQLite database for persistent storage</li>
</ul>

<hr>

<h2>2. PROJECT OVERVIEW</h2>
<h3>2.1 Problem Statement</h3>
<p>Educational institutions need an efficient way to identify students who may be at risk of poor academic performance early in the semester. Traditional methods of identifying at-risk students are often reactive rather than predictive. This project addresses the need for an automated, data-driven system that can:</p>
<ol>
<li>Store and manage student academic records</li>
<li>Predict final examination scores based on current performance</li>
<li>Classify students as "Safe" or "At Risk"</li>
<li>Provide visual analytics for administrators</li>
</ol>

<h3>2.2 Solution</h3>
<p>The SPPS provides a modern, intuitive web interface where educators can input student data, get instant AI-powered predictions, visualize class performance through charts, and export data for external analysis.</p>
