<h2>5. DATABASE DESIGN</h2>
<h3>5.1 Schema</h3>
<pre>CREATE TABLE students (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
  name TEXT NOT NULL,
  attendance REAL,
  midterm_1 INTEGER,
  midterm_2 INTEGER,
  previous_grade INTEGER,
  predicted_grade REAL,
  status TEXT
)</pre>

<h3>5.2 Sample Data Structure</h3>
<p>From the demo_students.csv (207 records):</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Field</th><th>Range</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td>name</td><td>String</td><td>Student full name</td></tr>
<tr><td>attendance</td><td>40-100%</td><td>Class attendance percentage</td></tr>
<tr><td>midterm_1</td><td>4-20</td><td>First midterm score (out of 20)</td></tr>
<tr><td>midterm_2</td><td>4-20</td><td>Second midterm score (out of 20)</td></tr>
<tr><td>previous_grade</td><td>40-98</td><td>Previous semester grade</td></tr>
<tr><td>predicted_grade</td><td>Calculated</td><td>AI-predicted final grade</td></tr>
<tr><td>status</td><td>Safe/At Risk</td><td>Classification result</td></tr>
</table>

