<h2>7. IMPLEMENTATION DETAILS</h2>
<h3>7.1 Server Implementation (server.ts)</h3>
<p>The Express server handles all API routes and serves the frontend:</p>
<ul>
<li>Database Initialization: Creates SQLite table if not exists</li>
<li>API Routes: CRUD operations for student management</li>
<li>Static File Serving: Serves built React app in production</li>
</ul>
<pre>
// Key API route - Bulk prediction update
app.put("/api/students/bulk", (req, res) => {
  const updates = req.body;
  const update = db.prepare("UPDATE students SET predicted_grade = ?, status = ? WHERE id = ?");
  const updateMany = db.transaction((data) => {
    for (const u of data) {
      update.run(u.predicted_grade, u.status, u.id);
    }
  });
  updateMany(updates);
  res.json({ success: true });
});</pre>

<h3>7.2 Frontend Implementation (App.tsx)</h3>
<p>The React application provides:</p>
<ul>
<li>Real-time data fetching with polling (5-second interval)</li>
<li>Animated UI with Motion library</li>
<li>CSV parsing with PapaParse library</li>
<li>Chart rendering with Recharts</li>
</ul>
<pre>
// Prediction algorithm
const W_ATTENDANCE = 0.2;
const W_MIDTERM_1 = 0.25;
const W_MIDTERM_2 = 0.35;
const W_PREVIOUS = 0.2;

const predictedGrade = Math.round(
  (student.attendance * W_ATTENDANCE) +
  (midterm1Normalized * W_MIDTERM_1) +
  (midterm2Normalized * W_MIDTERM_2) +
  (student.previous_grade * W_PREVIOUS)
);</pre>

